      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "POSH WHEELS (8) got the job done again after running them ragged making it three on end, scoring by one length (31.09) at this track over 530m. Well placed and will be tough to beat. JUNO USKO (1) has been in the money at her last two runs, most recently when third (22.70) in a Grade 6 over 395m at Murray Bridge. Expected to do much better this time. WILLOW TYSON (2) stalked the lead from a middle draw and boxed on well to finish 5.5 lengths back in third (30.83) at Gawler in a Grade 4/5 over 531m. Recorded one of the quickest times on the card last start despite being beaten. Bold showing expected. IMPRESS NEMO (7) is a last start winner in very good time. Worth consideration.",
